{ "Identifier":       {"ImplementerID": "IIDRA-assigned", "ImplementationID": "/* String from Implementer */", "AIMName": "PAF-RSR-V1.6"},
  "Header":            "PAF-RSR-V1.6",

  "APIProfile":       "Basic",
  "Description":      "Response and Scene Rendering: renders the machine's response - a Text - with an Avatar, the model to animate (for instance, chosen from a gallery). Text-To-Speech makes the Speech; Generative Face Description and Generative Body Description make the Face and Body Descriptors from the Text and the Speech; when a Personal Status is supplied, Personal Status De-multiplexing splits it into the Speech, Face and Body Personal Statuses that make them expressive. Speaking Avatar Synthesis makes the Speaking Avatar, ready to play. When Audio, a 3D Model and a Point of View are supplied, Scene and Avatar Rendering places the Speaking Avatar in the scene: a Basic Audio Scene and a Basic Visual Scene, or a Basic Audio-Visual Scene and the 3D Model Scene. RSR produces data; it does not play or draw.",

